menu "Michi Music Stream Display"

    config MICHI_DISPLAY_TASK_STACK_BYTES
        int "Display render task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 2048 16384
        help
          Stack of the render task (ESP-IDF xTaskCreate takes bytes). The
          task draws into the PSRAM framebuffer and flushes it to the panel
          (a full-frame flush is ~65-80 ms at 20 MHz SPI), so the stack also
          covers the esp_lcd draw_bitmap call. Raise it only if a future
          screen needs deeper frames.

    config MICHI_DISPLAY_QUEUE_LEN
        int "Render request queue length (requests)"
        default 4
        range 2 32
        help
          Depth of the FreeRTOS queue between the state observer /
          update_now_playing / request_redraw producers and the render task.
          A request dropped while the queue is full is logged (warn) by the
          producer and sets a pending flag; the task re-renders once more
          after the drain when the flag is set, and the next state change
          re-renders anyway, so a dropped request does not leave the screen
          stale (a drop racing that re-render is covered by the next state
          change).

    choice MICHI_DISPLAY_FONT_FAMILY
        prompt "UI font family"
        default MICHI_DISPLAY_FONT_INTER
        help
          Select the bitmap font family for all on-screen text. Both fonts
          cover the same 192-glyph charset (ASCII + Latin-1 + ellipsis)
          and share the same five size variants (XS / SM / MD / LG / PIN).
          The bitmaps are pre-rendered and committed; changing this option
          requires re-running tools/gen_michi_ui_assets.py with the
          appropriate --font flag.

        config MICHI_DISPLAY_FONT_INTER
            bool "Inter"
            help
              Inter (SIL Open Font License) - tight metrics, excellent
              legibility at small sizes on 320x240 landscape panels.

        config MICHI_DISPLAY_FONT_NOTO_SANS
            bool "Noto Sans"
            help
              Noto Sans (SIL Open Font License) - wide Unicode coverage,
              good for multilingual content.

    endchoice

    config MICHI_DISPLAY_RASTER_2BIT
        bool "Enable 2-bit anti-aliased raster mode"
        default y
        help
          When enabled the font bitmaps use 2-bit coverage values (0-3)
          instead of 1-bit on/off. Each coverage level is alpha-blended
          against the background at render time, producing smoother glyph
          edges at small point sizes on the RGB565 panel.
          Requires regenerating assets with --raster 2bit flag.
          Enabled by default for production builds.

endmenu
